WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:07.490
Just outside of Munich lies a sleepy village
called Fuggerei, where the rent for a whole

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.540
year is just under one Euro, 88 cents to be
precise.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.260
So what do you get in exchange for your measly
rent?

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.800
A matchbox?

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.800
A cupboard maybe?

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.009
Is it made of strudel?

00:00:20.009 --> 00:00:24.730
No, you get a modestly spacious two-bedroom
apartment made of stone.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:25.859
Is it in a dodgy area?

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:30.630
No, Fuggerei is extremely safe and rather
pretty if you ask me.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:35.730
It even sits inside its own walled enclave;
people pay millions for that shit in America.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:41.340
The five gates of Fuggerei are locked every
day at 10pm, blocking off any passage in or

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.280
out of the housing complex.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:48.000
The residents have to take turns to man a
gatehouse to let stragglers in after 10pm

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.420
who got locked outside, all of whom have to
pay a fee of 1 Euro for coming home late.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.140
What time do you call this Steve?

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.140
But bu…

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.740
Listen Steve, I don’t care if your car broke
down on your way to visit your terminally

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:01.740
ill grandma.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.460
It’s 2 minutes past 10, that’ll be one
year’s rent please.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.940
Why is the rent so cheap anyway?

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:13.460
Well Fuggerei is the world’s oldest social
housing complex still in use.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:19.540
Fuggerei sits in the Bavarian city of Augsburg
and it was created in 1520 to house the city’s

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:26.570
poorest residents, the rent was set at 1 Rhein
guilder when it was built, about 88 Euro cents

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:30.740
in todays money, and it hasn’t changed since.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:36.690
The owners, which are still the same family
that built the complex in 1520, have basically

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.100
put a big middle finger up to inflation.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:44.160
Fuggerei was built by a rather interesting
bloke and one of the richest persons to have

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:51.130
ever lived, Jakob Fugger, from the little
known but highly influential Fugger family

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:54.210
- but more about him in a minute.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:59.080
Altogether there are 52 identical houses in
Fuggerei, each divided into apartments.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.090
There’s also a town square and a church.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:06.020
But wait a minute, before you go and tell
your mum you’ve found a place of your own

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.149
and you’re moving to Germany.

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:12.609
Because unfortunately, you’re probably not
allowed to live there.

00:02:12.609 --> 00:02:14.730
Yeah sorry, sit back down.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:20.389
If the rent sounds too good to be true, that’s
because there are strict rules for anyone

00:02:20.389 --> 00:02:26.189
wanting to rent their very own slice of this
super-cheap gated community.

00:02:26.189 --> 00:02:31.170
To rent an apartment here one must have lived
at least two years in Augsburg, belong to

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.430
the Catholic faith and be extremely poor,
without any debt.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:43.529
No only that, once you live in Fuggerei, you
are required to say three prayers every day,

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:49.120
thanking the Fugger family for allowing you
to live there and you also must pray for their

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.120
souls.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.700
This place is like a cult.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.989
People usually have a grave dislike for bankers,
which the residents of Fuggerei all agree

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:57.989
with.

00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:02.389
But when residents were asked about their
opinion of the Fugger family, whom themselves

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:07.239
were billionaire bankers, their opinion quickly
changes.

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:12.019
The residents here have nothing but endless
good words to say about Jakob Fugger and his

00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:16.209
family, upholding them almost as deities.

00:03:16.209 --> 00:03:19.749
Maybe they’re just grateful for the fact
they have a house in a rather lovely city

00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:22.049
for just under one Euro per year.

00:03:22.049 --> 00:03:26.159
Or maybe it’s the fact that they will be
chucked out of Fuggerei if they say otherwise.

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:31.749
Hmm, I’m starting to think they should rename
this place to “Little North Korea”.

00:03:31.749 --> 00:03:36.349
I’m exaggerating of course, it’s not that
bad; “I’m sorry lord Fugger, please don’t

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.069
evict my grandma!”.

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:43.329
So who is Jakob Fugger, why was he so wealthy
and why did he create Fuggerei?

00:03:43.329 --> 00:03:49.620
The Fugger family are a prominent family of
European bankers who took over the infamous

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.950
Medici family.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:56.469
Jakob Fugger was the wealthiest of the family
and he was commonly referred to as “Jakob

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:59.269
the Rich” by all who knew him.

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:03.170
Jakob started out in the textile industry,
trading with Italy.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:08.959
He then invested in mining and soon came to
control a huge portion of the silver and copper

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:11.860
mining operations throughout Europe.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:18.170
Jakob also owned a bank and actually minted
coins for the Vatican, which enabled him to

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:23.729
control the catholic faith and thusly control
European politics, because at that time, the

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:27.250
pope had his fingers in all those juicy political
pies.

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:32.659
For a short while Jakob’s wealth made his
home city of Augsburg the banking capital

00:04:32.659 --> 00:04:34.159
of Europe.

00:04:34.159 --> 00:04:42.909
Jakob was worth the modern equivalent of $277
billion, if he was alive today he would be

00:04:42.909 --> 00:04:47.289
the richest person in the world, by a mile.

00:04:47.289 --> 00:04:54.139
But he was no saint, Jakob’s path to riches
was paved with deceit and political corruption,

00:04:54.139 --> 00:04:58.139
some say he was even worse than the highly
corrupt Medicis.

00:04:58.139 --> 00:05:04.259
He even created his own weekly newspaper,
just for his eyes, that contained dirt on

00:05:04.259 --> 00:05:07.560
his competitors, so he could get ahead of
them.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:13.139
He paid a lot of money for the newspaper to
be researched, printed and delivered to him

00:05:13.139 --> 00:05:15.030
every week.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:20.099
One week he must have read some dirt on himself
in his own newspaper, because in an effort

00:05:20.099 --> 00:05:25.710
to dispel the bad press surrounding him, and
improve his public image, Jakob created the

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:31.669
social housing complex of Fuggerei to house
the poorest of Augsburg’s citizens and he

00:05:31.669 --> 00:05:36.520
made the rent so ridiculously low, at 1 Rhein
guilder, that anyone could afford to live

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:37.520
there.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.330
So why was Fuggerei created?

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:45.449
So a ruthless capitalist could try to persuade
the world that he was really quite a nice

00:05:45.449 --> 00:05:46.449
guy.

00:05:46.449 --> 00:05:51.400
Hey, it seems to have worked, even today the
residents of Fuggerei literally worship Jakob

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:52.870
and the Fugger family.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:58.289
They’ve even opened a museum there to showcase
the legacy of the Fugger family.

00:05:58.289 --> 00:06:01.139
So would you live in Fuggerei if you could?

00:06:01.139 --> 00:06:04.969
All you have to do is worship a false deity
that’s been dead for 500 years.

00:06:04.969 --> 00:06:35.320
Oh and don’t come home after 10 o’clock,
they still haven’t forgiven Steve.

